WEBVTT

00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:01.899
This is the payments portal for the

00:00:01.942 --> 00:00:04.459
orchestrator, Unicity's in-house payment service.

00:00:05.227 --> 00:00:06.934
The Payments team sets it up and runs

00:00:06.977 --> 00:00:08.257
it here, without a developer.

00:00:08.939 --> 00:00:10.134
Nine pages are working today,

00:00:10.561 --> 00:00:11.585
and they do three jobs:

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:13.718
connect, route, and see.

00:00:15.699 --> 00:00:16.399
Job one:

00:00:16.595 --> 00:00:17.295
connect.

00:00:17.533 --> 00:00:19.453
Processors is where Payments connects our

00:00:19.496 --> 00:00:20.196
merchant accounts.

00:00:20.691 --> 00:00:21.715
Six are connected today,

00:00:22.312 --> 00:00:24.829
across Worldpay, Nuvei, Braintree for

00:00:24.872 --> 00:00:26.323
PayPal, and Network Merchants.

00:00:26.742 --> 00:00:28.278
For each account we choose its markets,

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:29.942
card brands and wallets,

00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:32.161
test the connection, and switch it on.

00:00:32.758 --> 00:00:34.550
Adding another takes three short steps.

00:00:36.216 --> 00:00:38.520
Checkout previews the payment form exactly

00:00:38.733 --> 00:00:39.629
as a shopper sees it.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.982
Pick a market, and the portal shows the

00:00:42.024 --> 00:00:43.944
ways to pay there and the billing address

00:00:44.072 --> 00:00:45.395
in that country's own layout,

00:00:45.651 --> 00:00:47.315
at desktop or mobile size.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.046
You can type into it, and nothing is sent.

00:00:51.756 --> 00:00:53.505
Settings holds the websites allowed to

00:00:53.548 --> 00:00:55.724
show that form, and the keys our servers

00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:57.857
use, one for test and one for production.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.929
A key is shown once, and rotating gives

00:01:01.015 --> 00:01:02.508
the old key twenty-four hours,

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:04.855
so a change never breaks checkout.

00:01:06.146 --> 00:01:07.981
Team lists everyone who can sign in.

00:01:08.279 --> 00:01:10.413
An admin invites a teammate by link,

00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:12.034
as a member or an admin.

00:01:12.333 --> 00:01:14.338
A member sees everything and drafts

00:01:14.423 --> 00:01:15.123
routing rules;

00:01:15.362 --> 00:01:17.026
an admin also changes the setup.

00:01:17.314 --> 00:01:18.594
Everyone has their own login,

00:01:18.935 --> 00:01:20.428
so every change carries a name.

00:01:22.076 --> 00:01:22.776
Job two:

00:01:23.057 --> 00:01:23.757
route.

00:01:23.825 --> 00:01:25.873
Routing decides which processor account

00:01:25.959 --> 00:01:26.897
charges each payment.

00:01:27.452 --> 00:01:29.031
Pick a market and a kind of payment,

00:01:29.372 --> 00:01:30.097
then build the rules.

00:01:30.565 --> 00:01:32.613
A rule can send everything to one account,

00:01:32.912 --> 00:01:34.789
or split it across several by share,

00:01:35.216 --> 00:01:36.667
with failover to the next account,

00:01:37.008 --> 00:01:39.184
and a fallback for anything no rule matches.

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:42.189
Before anything is published,

00:01:42.615 --> 00:01:44.919
the portal lists where every card brand

00:01:45.175 --> 00:01:47.309
and wallet would land, and Try a payment

00:01:47.394 --> 00:01:49.101
runs a dry run that charges nothing.

00:01:49.911 --> 00:01:51.746
More than forty dry runs so far,

00:01:52.045 --> 00:01:53.965
and every one went where the rules said.

00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:56.210
Then save a draft, publish,

00:01:56.508 --> 00:01:58.002
and every version is kept.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:00.386
Job three:

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:01.367
see.

00:02:01.649 --> 00:02:03.185
Payments lists every payment.

00:02:03.526 --> 00:02:05.531
Open one, and every attempt is there:

00:02:05.958 --> 00:02:07.025
the processor that took it,

00:02:07.323 --> 00:02:08.023
and how it ended.

00:02:08.646 --> 00:02:10.139
This one was paid on its third attempt.

00:02:10.509 --> 00:02:12.557
Orders shows the same payment under our

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.861
own order reference, and finds an order by

00:02:14.904 --> 00:02:17.976
reference, email, or a card's last four digits.

00:02:19.656 --> 00:02:21.789
Webhooks are the signed messages that tell

00:02:21.832 --> 00:02:23.795
our systems what happened to each payment.

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:25.587
Here is the one for that payment:

00:02:25.971 --> 00:02:28.104
delivered, with the reply exactly as

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:29.853
received, and it can be sent again.

00:02:30.309 --> 00:02:32.186
The page also holds the endpoints these

00:02:32.272 --> 00:02:33.808
messages go to, both verified.

00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:37.195
And the Dashboard adds it all up.

00:02:37.664 --> 00:02:40.821
Pick today, seven, thirty or ninety days,

00:02:41.248 --> 00:02:43.168
and each figure compares itself with the

00:02:43.211 --> 00:02:45.173
period before, including payments that

00:02:45.216 --> 00:02:46.539
succeeded after a decline.

00:02:47.004 --> 00:02:48.924
A switch in the header moves every page

00:02:49.095 --> 00:02:50.332
between Test and production.

00:02:52.186 --> 00:02:53.679
That is the payments portal for the

00:02:53.722 --> 00:02:54.422
orchestrator today.

00:02:55.002 --> 00:02:56.922
Payments connects the processor accounts,

00:02:57.306 --> 00:02:59.525
sets, tests and publishes the routing,

00:02:59.866 --> 00:03:02.255
and sees every payment, attempt and

00:03:02.298 --> 00:03:03.935
webhook in one place.

